  "title": "BT-DHT: Fix infinite loop in malformed error packets",
  "description": "If the int or string that is part of the error returns 0 (indicating\nfailure) then return zero. Commit 6f30bc471346e3e2ce3df1e13d873669fa94c951\nfixed an off-by-one error in returning the end offset of an error, but\nthat caused 1 instead of 0 to be returned from dissect_bt_dht_error,\nleading to stack overflows and infinite loops in the case of a badly\nformatted error.\n\nFix #19277.",
